        <body>
            <div xml:id="d235">

                <pb facs="0307" n="231" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg231"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1892</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Russell to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 107</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 26, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith
                    English and Spanish text of the proclamation issued by Rear Admiral Caperton in
                    regard to the advance of our forces on Santiago.</p>
                <p>The 4th Regiment of Marines, Colonel J. H. Pendleton, arrived here on the 18th
                    instant, and left on the evening of the 19th for Monte Cristi, and are now on
                    the march to Santiago, where they will arrive in three or four days.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William W. Russell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d235-a1.xml" xpointer="d235-a1"/>
            </div>
